~ start
Hadrik Vale: The Registry Archive has three doors, two locks, and one clerk on duty. The third door is for things that have not happened yet.
=> hub

~ hub
- "Have you filed a reflection that remembers me?" [if NGPlus.is_active(SaveGame.ng_plus) /]
	Hadrik Vale: The third door recorded your arrival before you returned. I have not decided which entry is the copy.
	=> hub
- "What is the Registry watching in this district?" [if not GameState.get_flag("dom_registry_notice_seen") /]
	do GameState.set_flag("dom_registry_notice_seen", true)
	do Reputation.record("player", "the-registry", 1.0, "Asked what the Registry was watching in Dom", "dom")
	Hadrik Vale: Names, thresholds, missing cargo, and any object that survives an explanation. The bell house is on the list now. So is the east road.
	=> END
- "The bell house is not a failure." [if GameState.get_flag("dom_bellhouse_inspected") and not GameState.get_flag("dom_registry_challenged") /]
	do GameState.set_flag("dom_registry_challenged", true)
	do Reputation.record("player", "the-registry", -2.0, "Challenged the Registry's failure mark on the Dom bell house", "dom")
	Hadrik Vale: Then submit a better word before someone else submits a final one. We do not punish accuracy. We punish unfiled accuracy.
	=> END
- "Could the Registry open the stacks to me?" [if Reputation.band("the-registry") == "warm" or Reputation.band("the-registry") == "allied" /]
	Hadrik Vale: For you, the second door. Your filings have been accurate, which around here passes for devotion. Touch nothing with a red seal.
	=> hub
- "You keep looking at me like a misfiled entry." [if Reputation.band("the-registry") == "cold" or Reputation.band("the-registry") == "hostile" /]
	Hadrik Vale: The Registry does not glare. It annotates. Your margin is getting crowded — consider filing something we can approve of.
	=> hub
- "I need a quiet place to read."
	Hadrik Vale: Quiet is available by appointment. Reading is available if you do not touch the numbered drawers.
	=> END
